$\begin{align}
&\phantom{=}\dfrac{-5x^2+20x}{x^3-3x^2-4x}
\\\\
&=\dfrac{-5x(x-4)}{x(x-4)(x+1)}\qquad\gray{\text{Factor numerator & denominator}}
\\\\
&=\dfrac{-5\cancel {x}\cancel{(x-4)}}{{\cancel {x}\cancel{(x-4)}(x+1)}}\qquad\gray{\text{Cancel out common factors}}
\\\\
&=\dfrac{-5}{x+1}, \text{ for }x\neq 0,4
\end{align}$
